 See also the CIELO collaboration paper  NDS 148, 189 (2018)      2631 1451
 and the ENDF/B-VIII.0 paper NDS 148, 1 (2018).                   2631 1451
                                                                  2631 1451
 The evaluation was performed up to 150 MeV for 7 subsequent      2631 1451
 neutron emissions, 3 proton emissions and a single alpha-        2631 1451
 particle, deuteron, triton, and 3He for a total of 146 residual  2631 1451
 nuclei. Only 5 of these were treated as exclusive, i.e., had an  2631 1451
 explicit reaction assigned to them along with the corresponding  2631 1451
 exclusive spectra for all particles and gammas. The exclusive    2631 1451
 reactions were (n,g), (n,elas), (n,inel), (n,2n), (n,p), and (n, 2631 1451
 2p). For all the remaining we provide cross sections for residua 2631 1451
 production which represent a sum of contributions from all       2631 1451
 possible reactions populating a given residue. Their respective  2631 1451
 spectra are lumped together providing only seven cumulative      2631 1451
 spectra (for gammas, neutrons, protons, alphas, deuterons,       2631 1451
 tritons, and 3He) for all the inclusive channels.                2631 1451
                                                                  2631 1451
                                                                  2631 1451
 Development of the evaluation is traced in the                   2631 1451
 CIELO-iron project on the NNDC GForge server:                    2631 1451
 https://ndclx4.bnl.gov/gf/project/cielo_iron                     2631 1451
 All elements of the evaluation, such as experimental datasets,   2631 1451
 EMPIRE inputs and outputs, intermediate ENDF files and plots     2631 1451
 can be followed there in a chronological order.                  2631 1451
