 EXPERIMENTAL DATBASE                                             2631 1451
 --------------------                                             2631 1451
 Many measurements exist for the natural element, as well as for  2631 1451
 the major isotopic constituent 56Fe. This wealth of precise and  2631 1451
 high resolution experiments on a relatively light (A < 60)       2631 1451
 target reveals strong fluctuations that persist in total, and    2631 1451
 inelastic cross sections up to about 7 MeV. These fluctuations   2631 1451
 have to be incorporated in the evaluation and there is currently 2631 1451
 no theoretical model capable of reproducing such fluctuating     2631 1451
 behavior. Therefore, the experimental data, which always form    2631 1451
 the basis for the evaluation work, are even more critical in the 2631 1451
 case of iron. The current evaluation below 4 MeV is essentially  2631 1451
 fully based on the experimental data, while at higher energies   2631 1451
 EMPIRE calculations adjusted to reproduce available measurements 2631 1451
 were adopted.                                                    2631 1451
                                                                  2631 1451
 The experimental database used in the evaluation is summarized   2631 1451
 in Table IX of the primary reference (NDS 148,241(2018)). In     2631 1451
 doing this selection we favored: (i) broad energy range covered  2631 1451
 by the experiment, (ii) high energy resolution, and (iii) high   2631 1451
 (but reasonable) accuracy of the experiment. Thus the            2631 1451
 measurements providing possibly wide and reliable picture were   2631 1451
 given precedence over single energy-point experiments,           2631 1451
 especially within the energy range where strong fluctuations     2631 1451
 were observed. On the other hand, many single- or a few-point    2631 1451
 measurements adopted when no extended datasets were              2631 1451
 available. Some of the measured datasets were renormalized to    2631 1451
 account for changes in the reference cross sections since they   2631 1451
 were used in the analysis of the experiments. The                2631 1451
 renormalizations built into the EXFOR retrieval system were      2631 1451
 adopted. In case of the 56Fe(n,p) reaction we took advantage of  2631 1451
 the existing high quality evaluations available from the IRDFF   2631 1451
 library (INDC(NDS)-0616, IAEA, Vienna (2012)) and used these     2631 1451
 data instead of the actual measurements.                         2631 1451
                                                                  2631 1451
