   MT=151 Resolved resonances                                     2631 1451
       The Reich-Moore formula was used. Paremeters were evaluated2631 1451
       by Froehner's for JEF-2-2  but were taken from JENDL-4.0.  2631 1451
       Between 500 and 850 keV, background cross sections were    2631 1451
       applied to the elastic and capture cross sections          2631 1451
       to account for the missing resonances.                     2631 1451
       The following changes were done compared to JENDL-4.0:     2631 1451
         - Removed spurious p-wave resonance at 59.8 keV          2631 1451
         - Background reduced by 40% (capture, elastic)           2631 1451
           The difference was assigned to the elastic.            2631 1451
         - Corrected resonance energy 7.67240+5 to 7.667240+5 eV  2631 1451
         - Between 10 eV and 100 keV background was added         2631 1451
           to capture to make the cross section approximately     2631 1451
           follow the 1/v behaviour. The difference was           2631 1451
           compensated by the total cross section.                2631 1451
