 CROSS SECTION COVARIANCES                                        2631 1451
 -------------------------                                        2631 1451
                                                                  2631 1451
 MF=33                                                            2631 1451
                                                                  2631 1451
   For the nonthreshold reactions, the resonance part of the      2631 1451
   covariance matrix was estimated from the uncertainties of      2631 1451
   the resonance parameters given in the Atlas of Neutron         2631 1451
   Resonances by S. Mughabghab. (version 2016). If such           2631 1451
   uncertainties were missing in the Atlas an educated guess      2631 1451
   based on average parameter uncertainties has been used.        2631 1451
   The uncertainties of the negative resonance parameters were    2631 1451
   set at the values that reproduce uncertainties of the          2631 1451
   thermal constants. The uncertainty of the scattering radius    2631 1451
   was taken into account. Following general practice, strong     2631 1451
   correlation was assumed among the gamma widths.                2631 1451
   Then the resonance module of the EMPIRE code was used to       2631 1451
   produce file MF=32. This file has been processed with          2631 1451
   NJOY-2016 code to produce covariances for the cross            2631 1451
   sections which were incorporated in the final evaluation       2631 1451
   along with the covariances for the fast neutron region.        2631 1451
   In case of capture two uncertainty backgrounds were added:     2631 1451
   (i) 2% between 1 and 500 keV to control minimum                2631 1451
   uncertainties in the resolved resonance region and (ii) 20%    2631 1451
   between 500 and 850 keV to compensate for the missing          2631 1451
   resonances in this region.                                     2631 1451
                                                                  2631 1451
   Covariances were determined using Kalman filter-inspired       2631 1451
   Bayesian update procedure. This methodology combines           2631 1451
   experimental uncertainties with the model constraints          2631 1451
   imposed through the sensitivity profiles provided by the       2631 1451
   EMPIRE code. Using KALMAN, the model parameters were           2631 1451
   sequentially adjusted to each considered experiment.           2631 1451
   Cross section covariances are obtained by propagating          2631 1451
   covariances of the model parameters.                           2631 1451
   The covariances were computed for the major reaction           2631 1451
   channels represented in the evaluations: total, elastic,       2631 1451
   inelastic, capture, (n, 2n), and (n, p). Inelastic             2631 1451
   scattering to individual discrete levels (MT=51,...,90)        2631 1451
   and to the continuum (MT=91) were combined together into       2631 1451
   MT=4. In addition, covariances for the sum of all the          2631 1451
   remaining channels (MT=5) are provided. Experimental           2631 1451
   uncertainties reported in EXFOR, if available,                 2631 1451
   were used to determine the long-range correlations in the      2631 1451
   experimental covariance matrices.  If such information was     2631 1451
   not available from EXFOR default 45% correlation between       2631 1451
   different energy points for the same reaction was adopted.     2631 1451
   The experimental datasets showing pronounced fluctuation       2631 1451
   structure were smoothed before being used. Datasets with       2631 1451
   excessive number of energy points were thinned to keep         2631 1451
   the total number of points below 1000 per experiment.          2631 1451
                                                                  2631 1451
   In the case of (n,p) reaction where IRDFF cross sections       2631 1451
   were used in the evaluation procedure in place of the          2631 1451
   experimental datasets it was desirable to retain, as far       2631 1451
   as possible, also IRDFF covariances. We preserved KALMAN       2631 1451
   created covariances but during the procedure, we adjusted      2631 1451
   weights of the IRDFF cross sections to reproduce, as           2631 1451
   closely as possible, the original IRDFF uncertainties.         2631 1451
